--TEST--
`streamAs<T>` answers `Core\Db\Stream` at the class its call site wrote, which is not the `Core\Db\Rows` the buffering half of the same pair answers — `rule:core-classes/db-streaming`, `rule:core-classes/db-statement-members`, spec § 18
--FILE--
<?nvs
// § 18 puts four hydrating readings of one statement on `Core\Db\Queryable`,
// and the two axes are independent: `query`/`stream` decides where the rows
// are, and the written type argument decides what each row becomes. So the
// answer's *class* is the walk's and its *type argument* is the call site's,
// and a program that confuses the first axis for the second is refused here
// rather than at the row that would not arrive.
// covers: Core\Db\Connection::streamAs
use Core\Db\Derive;
use Core\Db\Transaction;

#[Derive]
class Person {
    public uint $id;
    public tainted string $name;

    public function constructor(uint $id, tainted string $name)
    {
        $this->id = $id;
        $this->name = $name;
    }
}

// `rule:classes/no-traits` declares the member once, so a transaction answers
// exactly what its connection does — this function type-checks, and is the
// agreement half of the refusal below.
class People {
    public static function walking(Transaction $tx): Core\Db\Stream<Person>
    {
        return $tx->streamAs<Person>("select id, name from people", []);
    }
}

var $db = Core\Db::connect("main");

Core\Db\Rows<Person> $wrong = $db->streamAs<Person>("select id, name from people", []);
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `Core\Db\Rows<Person>`, found `Core\Db\Stream<Person>`
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
